# Repository Layout

## Directory Structure

```
dnsscienced/                    (public repo - github.com/straticus1/dnsscienced)
├── cmd/                        dnsscienced binaries
├── internal/                   core DNS server logic
├── examples/                   example zone files
├── zones/                      ⚠️ SEPARATE PRIVATE REPO (not tracked here)
│   └── *.dnszone              90+ production zone files
└── LAYOUT                      this file
```

## Zones Directory Setup

The `zones/` directory contains private infrastructure details and is maintained
in a separate private repository.

### Initial Setup

```bash
# Clone main repo
gh repo clone straticus1/dnsscienced
cd dnsscienced

# Clone private zones repo into zones/ subdirectory
gh repo clone afterdarksys/dnsscienced-zones zones
```

### Working with Zones

The zones directory is a complete git repository:

```bash
cd zones/
git pull                        # get latest zone updates
# ... edit zone files ...
git add .
git commit -m "Update zone configuration"
git push                        # push to private repo
```

### Repository URLs

- **Public repo**: https://github.com/straticus1/dnsscienced
- **Private zones**: https://github.com/afterdarksys/dnsscienced-zones

## Why Separate Repos?

Zone files contain:
- Internal IP addresses
- Complete domain portfolio
- Subdomain infrastructure details
- DNS record configurations

These should not be exposed in the public open-source dnsscienced project.
